**Goal Model – Multi‑Robot Resource Delivery**

| Goal ID | Goal Title                     | Text (Human‑readable)                                                                                         | Runtime Annotation | Goal Type | Relation | Justification |
|---------|--------------------------------|-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------|---------------------|-----------|----------|---------------|
| G1      | Fulfill Resource Request       | Ensure that the requested resources are collected from storage and delivered to the requesting agent.              | `;`                | Achieve   | –        | The whole mission is achieved only after *both* collection and delivery are completed, therefore they must be performed sequentially. |
| G2      | Collect Resources              | Perform all actions needed to gather the required items from the storage locations.                               | `;`                | Perform   | AND (G1) | Collection must finish before delivery can start – a strict sequence. |
| G3      | Deliver Resources              | Perform all actions needed to transport the collected items to the specified destination.                           | `;`                | Perform   | AND (G1) | Delivery is the second half of the mission and must follow collection. |
| G4      | Determine Collection Order      | Query the system for the optimal visiting order of storages based on waiting‑time + path length.                 | `-`                 | Query     | AND (G2) | This is a pure information retrieval step that precedes any movement. |
| G5      | Navigate to Storage            | Move the robot from its current location to the chosen storage.                                                   | `-`                 | Perform   | AND (G2) | The robot must physically reach the storage before any request can be made. |
| G6      | Request Resource                | Send a request message to the storage with the exact specification of the needed items.                          | `-`                 | Perform   | AND (G2) | The request is the action that triggers the storage to prepare the items. |
| G7      | Wait for Retrieval            | Remain idle until the storage confirms that the items have been retrieved and are ready for pickup.              | `-`                 | Perform   | AND (G2) | Waiting is required before the robot can pick up the items. |
| G8      | Battery‑Low Handling (Collection) | If the battery falls below 10 % during collection, go to recharge and hand over the mission to another robot. | `;`                | Perform   | AND (G2) | The two sub‑tasks must happen in order: first recharge, then re‑assignment. |
| G9      | Go to Recharge Station         | Move the robot to the nearest recharging station.                                                               | `-`                 | Perform   | AND (G8) | Direct action needed when battery is low. |
| G10     | Assign Mission to Another Robot | Notify the central command and hand over the remaining collection task to a spare robot.                           | `-`                 | Perform   | AND (G8) | After recharging, the mission must be transferred. |
| G11     | Navigate to Destination         | Move the robot from its current location to the specified delivery point.                                       | `-`                 | Perform   | AND (G3) | The robot must reach the destination before it can hand over the items. |
| G12     | Transfer Resource              | Physically place the collected items into the delivery container or onto the receiving agent.                     | `-`                 | Perform   | AND (G3) | This is the core action of the delivery phase. |
| G13     | Battery‑Low Handling (Delivery) | If the battery falls below 30 % during delivery, return the resource to a checkpoint and hand over the rest of the task. | `;`                | Perform   | AND (G3) | The two sub‑tasks must happen in order: first return, then re‑assignment. |
| G14     | Return to Checkpoint           | Move the robot back to the nearest checkpoint with the resource still on board.                                   | `-`                 | Perform   | AND (G13) | Needed when battery is low during delivery. |
| G15     | Assign Remaining Task to Another Robot | Notify the central command and hand over the remaining delivery runs to a spare robot.                           | `-`                 | Perform   | AND (G13) | After returning, the mission must be transferred. |
| G16     | Failure Handling               | If the robot fails to return the resource to a checkpoint, trigger an alert and report to the sector manager. | `;`                | Perform   | AND (G13) | The two actions must occur in order: first alert, then report. |
| G17     | Trigger Alert                  | Send an alert message to the sector manager indicating the failure.                                           | `-`                 | Perform   | AND (G16) | Immediate notification is required. |
| G18     | Report to Sector Manager        | Send a detailed report of the failure and current status to the sector manager.                                 | `-`                 | Perform   | AND (G16) | The report follows the alert. |

