### Task Model – Concrete Actions

| Task ID | Task Title                     | Text (Human‑readable)                                                                 | Relation | Location          | Number of Robots | Justification |
|---------|--------------------------------|-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------|----------|-------------------|-------------------|---------------|
| AT1     | Navigate to Storage            | Move the robot to the storage location that holds the requested items.                      | AND (G5) | `storage`        | 1                 | One robot must perform the movement. |
| AT2     | Request Resource               | Send a request message to the storage with the exact specification of the needed items.   | AND (G6) | `storage`        | 1                 | Only the requesting robot is involved. |
| AT3     | Wait for Retrieval            | Remain idle until the storage confirms that the items are ready for pickup.                | AND (G7) | `storage`        | 1                 | The robot must wait at the storage. |
| AT4     | Go to Recharge Station         | Move the robot to the nearest recharging station when battery < 10 %.                         | AND (G9) | `recharge station` | 1                 | Only the low‑battery robot moves. |
| AT5     | Assign Mission to Another Robot | Notify central command and hand over the remaining collection task to a spare robot.         | AND (G10) | `central command` | `[1,n]`           | Multiple robots may be assigned; the number is variable. |
| AT6     | Navigate to Destination        | Move the robot from its current location to the specified delivery point.                   | AND (G11) | `destination`    | 1                 | One robot performs the movement. |
| AT7     | Transfer Resource              | Physically place the collected items into the delivery container or onto the receiving agent. | AND (G12) | `destination`    | 1                 | Only the delivering robot is involved. |
| AT8     | Return to Checkpoint          | Move the robot back to the nearest checkpoint with the resource still on board.             | AND (G14) | `checkpoint`    | 1                 | One robot performs the movement. |
| AT9     | Assign Remaining Task to Another Robot | Notify central command and hand over the remaining delivery runs to a spare robot.           | AND (G15) | `central command` | `[1,n]`           | Multiple robots may be assigned; the number is variable. |
| AT10    | Trigger Alert                  | Send an alert message to the sector manager indicating the failure to return the resource.  | AND (G17) | `robot's current location` | 1 | Only the failing robot sends the alert. |
| AT11    | Report to Sector Manager       | Send a detailed report of the failure and current status to the sector manager.           | AND (G18) | `sector manager` | 1 | Only the robot that detected the failure reports. |
| AT12    | Compute Collection Order       | Query the system for the optimal visiting order of storages based on waiting‑time + path length. | AND (G4) | `central command` | 1 | The central command calculates the order. |
| AT13    | Assign Robots to Parallel Collect‑Deliver Tasks | Notify central command and assign multiple robots to parallel collect‑deliver runs when multiple items are required. | AND (G2) | `central command` | `[1,n]` | Multiple robots can be assigned; the number is variable. |

